      "content": "I am currently conducting a preliminary review of the Q3 miscellaneous expenditure logs for our Stuttgart manufacturing facility. I've identified a series of low-value, non-standard transactions within the 'office supplies' category. These amounts are statistically insignificant on an individual basis and do not meet the threshold for a formal audit, yet they appear with a frequency that suggests they are not merely random clerical errors. \n\nWhat specific methodology would you recommend for distinguishing between benign administrative noise (such as rounding errors or unrecorded small-batch purchases) and deliberate, systematic patterns of unauthorized spending, without expanding the scope of the investigation?",
